gem:revenueCode a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    gem:prefLabel "Revenue Code" ;
    gem:description "A 'Revenue Code' is a string datatype property that contains the revenue code on a Medicare institutional claim - a four-digit code identifying the type of service or department (such as pharmacy, emergency room, or medical/surgical supplies)." ;
    gem:llmScopingNote """Revenue code (institutional); an external NUBC code set, not enumerated here. Claim/service-line runtime field; unpopulated in the current coverage-policy instance graph (see gem:MedicareClaim).""" ;
    rdfs:domain gem:BaseServiceLine ;
    rdfs:range  xsd:string ;
    gem:sourceAttribute "revenueCd" ;
    gem:memberOfOntology gem:gemOntology .

gem:ruleDescription a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    gem:prefLabel "Rule Description" ;
    gem:description "A 'Rule Description' is a string datatype property that captures one rule extracted from a CMS coverage policy — for example, an eligibility criterion, frequency limit, setting requirement, risk-factor enumeration, documentation requirement, or other evaluator criterion. Each rule is stored as a self-contained string in the policy's wording. A rule attaches exclusively to a gem:PolicyRule instance (the first-class form, S67+): the rule's verbatim text is carried on that instance via gem:ruleDescription, and gem:CMSpolicy or gem:AnchoredCodingScope (gem:PolicyGroup / gem:PolicyCodingRule) subjects link to it via gem:hasPolicyRule rather than carrying the string directly. The string form is intentionally non-atomic; future schema work will decompose rules into atomic component properties (deferred_proposals[72]). Domain history: generalized from PolicyGroup to AnchoredCodingScope at S60 (2026-06-15); extended to include gem:PolicyRule at S67 (2026-06-18); narrowed to gem:PolicyRule exclusively at S86 (2026-06-24) on completion of the Phase 4 schema closeout." ;
    gem:llmDetailedDefinition """THE load-bearing coverage-content field: the verbatim, NON-atomic text of one rule, carried on a gem:PolicyRule instance (domain is gem:PolicyRule exclusively since S86). Because the structured decomposition (gem:CoverageOutcome / qualifiers / atomic predicates) is deferred and unpopulated, this string is currently the primary source for what a rule requires or excludes. Read it together with the rule's gem:ruleType tag(s).""" ;
    gem:llmScopingNote """Free text; it may embed numeric thresholds and count/duration/frequency values (until gem:restrictionValue is codified), so parse from the string when a numeric criterion is needed. A gem:CMSpolicy or gem:AnchoredCodingScope reaches this text via gem:hasPolicyRule -> gem:PolicyRule, not by carrying the string directly.""" ;
    rdfs:domain gem:PolicyRule ;
    rdfs:range  xsd:string ;
    gem:memberOfOntology gem:gemOntology .

gem:sampleData a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    gem:prefLabel "Sample Data" ;
    gem:description "A 'Sample Data' is a string datatype property that contains an example of a data value found in this property. It is intended to be informative but is not a complete, inclusive list of valid values." ;
    gem:llmScopingNote """A documentation aid holding one illustrative example value for a property; informative only, not an exhaustive or authoritative list of valid values, and not a claim datum.""" ;
    rdfs:domain owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:range  xsd:string ;
    gem:memberOfOntology gem:gemOntology .

